course: dictionary
lesson: 15981
title: Uppish: too proud, or a risky shot
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. «Mia got uppish after she won the spelling bee, and she kept telling everyone she was cleverer than them all.» The clues are won, telling everyone and cleverer than them all. So uppish must mean acting too proud and better than others.
explain: Uppish is informal and a bit old-fashioned, and you hear it mostly in Britain. People often use it to tell someone off: «Don't get uppish with me!» That means "Don't be so proud and bossy with me."
explain: Uppish has a second meaning in cricket. An uppish shot goes high in the air and might be caught, so it is a risky shot. Same word, different meaning: look at the topic around it to know which meaning is right.
fact: «Uppish» means too proud and full of yourself, acting as if you are better than other people.
fact: «Uppish» is informal, mainly used in the UK, and sounds old-fashioned.
fact: Uppity means the same as uppish.
fact: In cricket, «uppish» describes a shot that goes up in the air and might be caught.
fact: A good check is to swap in your meaning: "Don't get too proud with me!" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
exercise: «Ava got uppish after she won the spelling bee and told everyone she was cleverer than them all.» What does uppish mean? | Glad to help others | Very tired after a long day | Quiet and shy | *Too proud and acting better than others
exercise: Dad says, «Don't get uppish just because you scored one goal!» What is Dad telling him not to do? | Run too slowly | *Be too proud and full of himself | Whistle at the referee | Go to bed early
exercise: In cricket, the commentator says, «That was an uppish shot, and the fielder has caught it!» What does uppish mean in cricket? | *A shot that goes high in the air and might be caught | A shot that goes along the ground very fast | A shot that hits the stumps
test: «Lily stopped being uppish when her friends told her she was showing off.» What does stopping being uppish mean? | Starting to sing | Going to sleep | Running faster | *Stopping being too proud
test: Which sentence uses uppish in the cricket sense? | *The batter played an uppish shot, and a fielder caught the ball. | Toad gets uppish whenever things go well for him. | Don't get uppish with me!
exam: Your friend says uppish is just a fancy word for happy. Is she right? | *No, it means too proud, not happy | Yes, it means glad and cheerful | No, it means too proud and acting better than others | Yes, it means the same as quiet
